{"action_count": 1, "component": "model", "config_id": "state-event-v1-group5-no-search-budget", "content": "The task requires diagnosing why the tutorial UI doesn't close and countdown UI doesn't appear when the player presses the interact key on the start screen. The causal chain involves interaction input → game state transition → OnStateChanged event publication → UI observer refresh.\n\nFrom the causal fact matrix, we see:\n- `GameInput.OnInteractAction` is declared and subscribed to by `KitchenGameManager.GameInput_OnInteraction`\n- `KitchenGameManager.GameInput_OnInteraction` writes to `state = State.CountdownToStart` but **does not publish** `OnStateChanged` (status: \"absent\" with repair_exemplar `OnStateChanged?.Invoke(this, EventArgs.Empty)`)\n- `TutorialUI.KitchenGameManager_OnStateChanged` subscribes to `OnStateChanged` and calls `Hide()`, but since the event isn't published during interaction, the UI never updates\n\nThe root cause is the missing event publication in `KitchenGameManager.GameInput_OnInteraction`. The smallest repair is to add `OnStateChanged?.Invoke(this, EventArgs.Empty)` after the state assignment.\n\nThe plan must include:\n- Objective: Fix missing OnStateChanged event publication during interaction\n- Hypotheses: Event publication missing in GameInput_OnInteraction handler\n- Required evidence: Confirm absence of OnStateChanged invocation in KitchenGameManager.cs line 42\n- Success criteria: Tutorial UI closes and countdown UI appears on interact\n- Validation: Compile check + PlayMode test to verify behavior\n\nSince the workflow requires validation_plan to include \"compile\" and \"playmode\", I'll submit a plan with those validation steps.\n\n", "duration_ms": 7819, "elapsed_ms": 24131, "event": "model_end", "model": "openai/qwen-plus", "monotonic_ns": 15985350614100, "outcome": "tool_call", "phase": "response", "round": 2, "run_id": "ablation-group5-run1-20260802-132611", "schema_version": "game-agent-jsonl-v3", "seq": 26, "ts"